+# ::a1 Explanatory Example Debate
+
+::a2 This document is itself a debate, and its subject is _Fair Debate_ — the platform you are looking at. ::a3 Reading it should be enough to understand how this place works.
+
+::a4 You are reading the opening _contribution_ of this debate. ::a5 Every contribution is split automatically into _statements_ — a sentence, a heading, a bullet point. ::a6 Each statement carries a key of its own and can therefore be referenced and answered on its own. ::a7 Hovering over a statement shows its key, clicking it shows its full URL.
+
+::a8 Statements that are highlighted have been answered already. ::a9 Click one to unfold the answers below it. ::a10 Most of this document lives in those answers, so unfolding them is how you read it.
+
+::a11 Parties are identified by letters, assigned in the order in which they join a debate.
+
+- ::a12 `a` is the party that opens the debate, which here is me.
+- ::a13 `b` is the first party to answer.
+- ::a14 `c` is the second party to answer.
+- ::a15 Further parties continue the alphabet, for as long as a debate attracts them.
+
+::a16 A party may also answer a statement of its own. ::a17 That is how a later addition gets a place of its own instead of quietly rewriting what was already published.
+
+::a18 Two properties set this platform apart from an ordinary comment section.
+
+1. ::a19 Persistent in-context answers.
+2. ::a20 Provable integrity of the content data.
\ No newline at end of file
